"Any NDEF tag can be the coin: a transit card, a hotel key, a blank. The app keeps a hash of the tag, never its contents. A copied tag is the same coin — the factor is possession, like every physical key ever cut. One honesty: NFC reading needs the NFC Tag Reading capability, which only a paid developer team's profile grants — under free Personal Team signing the taps will fail, and that is the team talking, not the tag." = "Cualquier etiqueta NDEF puede ser la moneda: una tarjeta de transporte, una llave de hotel, una en blanco. La app guarda un hash de la etiqueta, nunca su contenido: gastarla significa emparejar su presencia con un objetivo que elijas, con la cadencia como segundo factor.";
"Any time." = "Cuando quieras.";
"Any time. Genuinely." = "Cuando quieras. De verdad.";
"Anything else she builds: tools, scripts, whole programs — drafted by her minds, held here, yours to take anywhere. JavaScript runs on the spot." = "Todo lo demás que ella construye: herramientas, scripts, programas enteros — redactados por sus mentes, guardados aquí, tuyos para disparar.";
